# The affordance menu: what THIS agent could do, about what, and which way it moves things —
# one row per (means, property, lever), derived from the graph and nothing else.
#
# This is the Consulting member's prompt substrate, shipped before that member exists so the
# claim "the menu is derived, not written into a prompt" is checkable now (#127). It is also
# the reflex's worldview stated as data: every move the reflex can propose is a row here, and a
# move with no row is a move nothing should propose. A model handed these rows knows what a
# human authoring the world knew — you can look at moisture through this probe, you can raise
# it through this market — without a line of prose being maintained anywhere.
#
# `$me` is the one thing a shipped query cannot know, substituted as everywhere else. The
# patterns are unqualified on purpose: regions are public, wiring is public, and the T-Box's
# denomination and direction are public, so the menu spans them all through the default graph.
#
# What each branch asserts:
#   Observe — a sensor I poll, watching my subject, reporting this property. The lever is the
#             board; the direction column is empty because looking moves nothing.
#   Acquire — a market I bid in, WHOSE WINNINGS CAN PHYSICALLY REACH MY SUBJECT, whose GOOD a
#             valuation converts into this property and states which way the lot moves it. The
#             row is DEDUCED along the plumbing, link by link: the market's host holds an
#             actuator, the actuator is plumbed to my own pot, so opening it puts the good
#             where I am — and only the last link, that the good raises this property rather
#             than lowering it, is STATED, once, by the domain, because it is physics and no
#             topology can derive it. It used to trust the denomination alone, which with one
#             market was never caught lying — but an agent bidding in a market no valve
#             connects to its pot would have been offered a move that moves nothing, and a
#             second market (heat beside water) would have joined every market to every
#             property. The walk is what makes "this auction moves MY moisture" a conclusion.
#             The valuation joins through the venue's good (#198): venue -> marketFor ->
#             source -> supplies -> good <- ofGood <- valuation. Property alone stopped being
#             enough the day two venues priced one property in opposite directions — a fan
#             market lowering the moisture a water market raises would have put BOTH
#             directions on BOTH rows, four rows where the world holds two.
#   Apply   — deliberately absent, like everything about it: no held claim exists in a spot
#             market, so there is nothing to apply. The row arrives with the futures seam.
#
# A desire with NO row in this menu is the blind-or-helpless case: wanted, and either unseeable
# (desire:UnwatchedDesireShape warns at the gate) or unmovable (nothing warns yet — a want with
# no lever is legitimate, the temperature desire is exactly that, and the reflex simply never
# proposes for it). Unreachable now reads as unmovable too: a market whose deliveries cannot
# reach your pot is, for you, no lever at all.

SELECT ?means ?property ?via ?direction WHERE {
  $me desire:desires ?region ; ag:actsFor ?subject .
  ?region ssn:forProperty ?property .
  {
    $me sensing:polls ?via .
    ?via sensing:monitors ?subject ;
         sosa:observes ?property .
    BIND(intention:Observe AS ?means)
  } UNION {
    $me market:bidsIn ?via .
    ?via market:marketFor ?src .
    ?src market:supplies ?good .
    ?host market:hosts ?via ;
          actuation:hasActuator ?lever .
    ?lever actuation:actuates ?subject .
    ?valuation market:ofGood ?good ;
               market:aboutProperty ?property ;
               market:direction ?direction .
    BIND(intention:Acquire AS ?means)
  }
}
ORDER BY ?property ?means
